Thread priority at start: a thread created with a higher priority than its creator runs until it blocks.

- sys_ppu_thread_create waits (at most 200 ms, PS3_NO_PRIO_START=1 turns it off) until a new thread of higher
  priority than its creator has reached a blocking call (event queue receive, event flag, semaphore or condition
  wait, sleeps), as lv2's scheduler does. The game's SurMixer thread (prio 400, created by a prio 1000 thread)
  creates the event queue whose key its creator then hands to cellAudioSetNotifyEventQueue. Without the ordering
  the creator sometimes read a zero key, the mixer was never notified and the opening movie played without sound.

